.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-volume 1  "tapectl-volume " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume \- Manage volumes and tape operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage volumes and tape operations
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-init(1)
Initialize a new volume (write ID thunk to tape)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-write(1)
Write staged data to volume
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-resume(1)
Resume an interrupted write session (issue #25). Reload the SAME cartridge first: the session continues from its frozen staging files rather than rebuilding them, and it refuses (quarantining the volume) if the loaded tape\*(Aqs File 0 does not match, or if the tape is already sealed. There is no \-\-force: `volume write \-\-force` overrides a wrong\-cartridge finding before anything is written, which has no meaning for a tape this session has already partly written
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-abort(1)
Deliberately abandon a volume\*(Aqs unfinished write session (issue #94): `docs/design/layout\-session.md`\*(Aqs Aborted row, first clause. Use this when a `volume resume` reports a revalidation failure you know to be permanent (the staged data is really gone), or to clear a `planned` session that was killed before anything was written. Nothing can tell a transient cause from a permanent one but you, which is why resume never decides this on its own
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-verify(1)
Verify volume contents via the keyless chain walk (seal \-> front index \-> content). Default tier is `\-\-full` (integrity: hashes every content file); `\-\-quick` opts down to navigable (seal binding + front index self\-consistency only, no per\-file content hashing)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-identify(1)
Identify a tape (read ID thunk)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-move(1)
Move a volume to a location
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-retire(1)
Retire a volume (with impact analysis)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-read\-slices(1)
Read encrypted slices from a volume into staging (then use `volume write` to write them)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-compact\-read(1)
Read live encrypted slices from a volume to staging (compaction step 1)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-compact\-write(1)
Write compaction slices from staging to destination (compaction step 2)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-plan(1)
Show bin\-packing plan for pending staged data
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-compact\-finish(1)
Retire source volume after compaction (compaction step 3)
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-compact(1)
Interactive compaction: read + write + finish in one flow
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
